        "---\n",
        "title: Relationships Between Numerical Variables\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "filters:\n",
        "  - code-blanks\n",
        "\n",
        "code-blanks:\n",
        "  progressive-reveal: true\n",
        "  packages:\n",
        "    - dplyr\n",
        "    - ggplot2\n",
        "    - palmerpenguins\n",
        "  setup:\n",
        "    - library(ggplot2)\n",
        "    - library(dplyr)\n",
        "    - library(palmerpenguins)\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Penguin Scatterplots\n",
        "\n",
        "We will once again use the data about three species of penguins that live in the Palmer Archipelago, a set of Antarctic islands south of South America. This time, we're looking for relationships among the different body measurements of the penguins.\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll start by making a scatterplot with `body_mass_g` as the explanatory variable and `bill_length_mm` as the response variable.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: body_mass_g\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: bill_length_mm\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: geom_point\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(penguins) +\n",
        "  aes(x = body_mass_g, y = bill_length_mm) +\n",
        "  geom_point() + \n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"Relationship between body mass and bill length\",\n",
        "    x = \"Body mass (grams)\",\n",
        "    y = \"Bill length (millimeters)\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "Why do you think the geom for a scatterplot was named `geom_point`?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Fill in the blanks below to make a scatterplot with flipper length as the explanatory variable and body mass as the response variable.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: body_mass_g\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: geom_point\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(penguins) +\n",
        "  aes(x = flipper_length_mm, y = body_mass_g) +\n",
        "  geom_point() + \n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"Relationship between flipper length and body mass\",\n",
        "    x = \"Flipper length (millimeters)\",\n",
        "    y = \"Body mass (grams)\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "How would you describe the relationship between flipper length and body mass based on the scatterplot you just made?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The numerical variables in the dataset are `body_mass_g`, `bill_length_mm`, `bill_depth_mm`, and `flipper_length_mm`. Make one more scatterplot using two of these variables of your choice.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|  target: \"blank1\"\n",
        "#|  prefill: false\n",
        "#|  occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|  match: text\n",
        "\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|  target: \"blank2\"\n",
        "#|  prefill: false\n",
        "#|  occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|  match: text\n",
        "\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|  target: \"blank3\"\n",
        "#|  prefill: false\n",
        "#|  occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|  match: text\n",
        "\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|  target: \"blank4\"\n",
        "#|  prefill: false\n",
        "#|  occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|  match: text\n",
        "\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|  target: \"blank5\"\n",
        "#|  prefill: false\n",
        "#|  occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|  match: text\n",
        "\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|  target: geom_point\n",
        "#|  prefill: false\n",
        "#|  occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|  match: text\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(penguins) +\n",
        "  aes(x = \"blank1\", y = \"blank2\") +\n",
        "  geom_point() +\n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"blank3\",\n",
        "    x = \"blank4\",\n",
        "    y = \"blank5\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## Calculating Correlation\n",
        "\n",
        "The R function `cor()` for correlation works a bit differently than the other functions we've used so far. We retrieve the variable we want from the `penguins` dataset using `$`. For example, `penguins$body_mass_g` gives us the body mass column.\n",
        "\n",
        "Here's an example of finding the correlation between body mass and bill length:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: body_mass_g\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: bill_length_mm\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "cor(penguins$body_mass_g, penguins$bill_length_mm, \"pairwise.complete.obs\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "Does this correlation make sense with the scatterplot for these two variables at the beginning of the activity? Why?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Fill in the blanks below to find the correlation between flipper length and body mass.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: body_mass_g\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: flipper_length_mm\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "cor(penguins$body_mass_g, penguins$flipper_length_mm, \"pairwise.complete.obs\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## Adding a Categorical Variable to a Scatterplot\n",
        "\n",
        "Sometimes there's more to the story than a relationship between two numerical variables. Other variables might affect our results as well. For categorical variables with just a few values, we can add this information into our scatterplots.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, maybe I'm curious about whether a penguin's species affects how their body mass and bill length are related. I might make the following scatterplot:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: body_mass_g\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: bill_length_mm\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: species\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(penguins) +\n",
        "  aes(x = body_mass_g, y = bill_length_mm, color = species) +\n",
        "  geom_point() + \n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"Relationship between body mass and bill length\",\n",
        "    x = \"Body mass (grams)\",\n",
        "    y = \"Bill length (millimeters)\",\n",
        "    color = \"Species\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The aesthetic `color` affects the color of the dots in the scatterplot. Note that this is different from `fill`, which controlled the color of the bars in bar graphs or histograms! If you use `color` on a bar graph or histogram, it will color **only** the edges of the bar, not the inside.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "What new patterns (if any) do you notice in the scatterplot with the species information added?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The categorical variables in this dataset were `sex`, `species`, and `island`. Choose one of those and add it into the flipper length and body mass graph below.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: color\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 2\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: \"blank1\"\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank2\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(penguins) +\n",
        "  aes(x = flipper_length_mm, y = body_mass_g, color = \"blank1\") +\n",
        "  geom_point() + \n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"Relationship between flipper length and body mass\",\n",
        "    x = \"Flipper length (millimeters)\",\n",
        "    y = \"Body mass (grams)\",\n",
        "    color = \"blank2\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```"
